<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types>
    rdfs:label "AGS 4.2.0 Data Types"@en ;
    schema:description "The data TYPEs of AGS 4.2.0. Generic types such as nDP are top concepts; the specific types used in the dictionary (e.g. 2DP) are narrower concepts."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/0DP>
    rdfs:label "0DP: 0 decimal places"@en ;
    schema:description "Data type 0DP: 0 decimal places. A specific form of the generic type nDP (Value with required number of decimal places)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/1DP>
    rdfs:label "1DP: 1 decimal place"@en ;
    schema:description "Data type 1DP: 1 decimal place. A specific form of the generic type nDP (Value with required number of decimal places)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/1SCI>
    rdfs:label "1SCI: scientific notation with 1 decimal place"@en ;
    schema:description "Data type 1SCI: scientific notation with 1 decimal place. A specific form of the generic type nSCI (Scientific Notation with required number of decimal places)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/1SF>
    rdfs:label "1SF: 1 significant figure"@en ;
    schema:description "Data type 1SF: 1 significant figure. A specific form of the generic type nSF (Value with required number of significant figures)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/2DP>
    rdfs:label "2DP: 2 decimal places"@en ;
    schema:description "Data type 2DP: 2 decimal places. A specific form of the generic type nDP (Value with required number of decimal places)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/2SCI>
    rdfs:label "2SCI: scientific notation with 2 decimal places"@en ;
    schema:description "Data type 2SCI: scientific notation with 2 decimal places. A specific form of the generic type nSCI (Scientific Notation with required number of decimal places)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/2SF>
    rdfs:label "2SF: 2 significant figures"@en ;
    schema:description "Data type 2SF: 2 significant figures. A specific form of the generic type nSF (Value with required number of significant figures)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/3DP>
    rdfs:label "3DP: 3 decimal places"@en ;
    schema:description "Data type 3DP: 3 decimal places. A specific form of the generic type nDP (Value with required number of decimal places)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/3SF>
    rdfs:label "3SF: 3 significant figures"@en ;
    schema:description "Data type 3SF: 3 significant figures. A specific form of the generic type nSF (Value with required number of significant figures)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/4DP>
    rdfs:label "4DP: 4 decimal places"@en ;
    schema:description "Data type 4DP: 4 decimal places. A specific form of the generic type nDP (Value with required number of decimal places)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/DMS>
    rdfs:label "Degrees: Minutes: Seconds"@en ;
    schema:description "Degrees: Minutes: Seconds. e.g. 51: 28: 52.498"@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/DT>
    rdfs:label "Date time in international format"@en ;
    schema:description """Date time in international format. yyyy-mm-ddThh:mm:ss.sssZ(+hh:mm) or yyyy-mm-dd or hh:mm:ss or yyyy
This format may be used in full or part based on user requirements"""@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/ID>
    rdfs:label "Unique Identifier"@en ;
    schema:description """Unique Identifier. An ID is a unique identifier used across the project.
The ID shall be unique in the parent group but may be repeated in child groups i.e. SAMP (parent) vs ELRG (child), LOCA (parent) vs SAMP (child)."""@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/MC>
    rdfs:label "British Standard BS1377 : Part 2 reported moisture content"@en ;
    schema:description "British Standard BS1377 : Part 2 reported moisture content. This data type is included for legacy reasons and not used in AGS 4.2"@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/PA>
    rdfs:label "Text listed in ABBR Group"@en ;
    schema:description """Text listed in ABBR Group. Abbreviations listed in ABBR group. Rule 16 refers.
The list of standard abbreviations and descriptions are presented on the AGS website and shall not be redefined.
Other abbreviations may be defined as required within a project, but shall not match/impersonate existing standard abbreviations
e.g. "CP" for 'Cable percussion' in LOCA_TYPE shall not be given a non-standard abbreviation defined as "CH" for 'Cable hole'; likewise "SCP" (Static cone penetrometer) shall not be replaced by a non-standard abbreviation of "CPT" (Cone penetration test).
Multiple abbreviations can be used in a data VARIABLE. Where this occurs, abbreviations are joined using the concatenation character defined in TRAN_RCON (a "+" character by default)."""@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/PT>
    rdfs:label "Text listed in TYPE Group"@en ;
    schema:description "Text listed in TYPE Group. Abbreviations listed in TYPE group. Rule 17 refers."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/PU>
    rdfs:label "Text listed in UNIT Group"@en ;
    schema:description """Text listed in UNIT Group. Abbreviations listed in UNIT group. Rule 15 refers.
The list of standard units and descriptions are presented on the AGS website and shall not be redefined.
This list is case sensitive."""@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/RL>
    rdfs:label "Record Link"@en ;
    schema:description """Record Link. Rule 11 refers.
Text in specified format that refers to one or more records in other Groups by Key fields."""@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/T>
    rdfs:label "Elapsed Time"@en ;
    schema:description "Elapsed Time. e.g. hh:mm:ss"@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/U>
    rdfs:label "Value with a variable format"@en ;
    schema:description "Value with a variable format. This is used for fields that contain values with differing accuracy; e.g. AGS 4.1 = ELRG_RVAL (AGS 4.0 = ERES_RVAL)."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/X>
    rdfs:label "Text"@en ;
    schema:description "Text. Abbreviations used in text data are to be listed in ABBR group. Rule 16 refers."@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/XN>
    rdfs:label "Text/numeric"@en ;
    schema:description """Text/numeric. There are some measured parameters that are typically numeric but can have a valid result that is text; examples include plastic limit (34 or NP) and depth of water in a borehole (2.34 or dry).
Abbreviations used in text data are to be listed in ABBR group. Rule 16 refers."""@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/YN>
    rdfs:label "Yes or No"@en ;
    schema:description """Yes or No. Data in the file will be either a Y or N or Null (Rule 12)
e.g. Y"""@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/nDP>
    rdfs:label "Value with required number of decimal places"@en ;
    schema:description "Value with required number of decimal places. e.g. 2DP = 2 decimal places = 2.34"@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/nSCI>
    rdfs:label "Scientific Notation with required number of decimal places"@en ;
    schema:description "Scientific Notation with required number of decimal places. e.g. 73100 as 2SCI = 7.31E4; 73100 as 1SCI = 7.3E4"@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/nSF>
    rdfs:label "Value with required number of significant figures"@en ;
    schema:description "Value with required number of significant figures. e.g. 2SF = 2 significant figures = 1.2, 10"@en ;
.

<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/dictionary>
    rdfs:label "AGS 4.2.0 Groups and Headings"@en ;
    schema:description "The GROUPs and HEADINGs of the AGS 4.2.0 data dictionary (Electronic Transfer of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Data). Groups are top concepts and each heading is a narrower concept of every group it appears in. Group categories are collections."@en ;
.

